# Project initiation checklist

Copier wrote this project's files, and `scripts/bootstrap.py` creates its labels and standing trackers.
Neither can change the repository's settings or the agent harness's configuration, so the owner works through this list once, right after generating the project.
This file is the one copy of the checklist. `instructing-agents.md` explains the process around it.

## What the bootstrap script does, and how to confirm it

- [ ] **The bootstrap script has run with a narrow token.**
  Create a fine-grained personal access token limited to `{{ repo_owner }}/{{ repo_name }}` only, with Issues read and write (GitHub adds Metadata read); nothing else.
  Then run `GITHUB_TOKEN=<token> python3 scripts/bootstrap.py` (add `--dry-run` first to see what it would do).
  By default the script refuses a classic token, a fine-grained token that can see other private repositories, or an app installation token that can reach other repositories; pass `--allow-broad-token` to proceed with a warning instead, for the rare case a narrower token cannot be issued.
- [ ] **Labels exist.**
  The triage labels (`needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `needs-grilling`, `ready-for-structure`, `ready-for-feature-design`, `ready-for-build`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`, `needs-decision`), the categories (`bug`, `enhancement`), `epic`, the queue labels (`queued`, `in-flight`), the routing label `main-health`, the release-note labels (`release:user`, `release:integrator`, `release:internal`, `breaking`) and the parking labels (`hanging`, `deferred-accepted-risk`, `future`, `deferred-arch-finding`).
  Confirm with `gh label list --repo {{ repo_owner }}/{{ repo_name }}`.
- [ ] **The five standing trackers exist and their numbers are recorded** in `.copier-answers.yml` as `post_merge_review_tracker`, `deferred_ideas_epic`, `hanging_epic`, `arch_findings_epic` and `local_full_suite_evidence_tracker`.
- [ ] **The numbers are rendered into the rule files.**
  Run `copier recopy --trust --skip-tasks --defaults --overwrite` once, straight after bootstrap and before any local edits, then commit the result.
- [ ] **Workflows are manual-dispatch only.**
  Every file under `.github/workflows/` triggers on `workflow_dispatch` alone; the bootstrap script checks the local copies.
  Read them back after the first push and confirm none has a push, pull-request or schedule trigger.

## Repository settings, set by hand

- [ ] **Delete head branches on merge:** `gh repo edit {{ repo_owner }}/{{ repo_name }} --delete-branch-on-merge`
- [ ] **Vulnerability alerts on, advisory only:** `gh api -X PUT repos/{{ repo_owner }}/{{ repo_name }}/vulnerability-alerts`
  Leave automated security-update PRs and version-update PRs off: moving a pinned dependency is its own ticketed, reviewed change; file a ticket if you want either turned on.
- [ ] **Branch protection and merge method:** decide whether to protect `main` and which merge methods to allow.
  Whatever you set must still let a build thread merge its own PR once its review gate is clear, since agents self-merge.
- [ ] **Organisation defaults:** check the Actions settings page for any default workflows your organisation applies.
- [ ] **Secrets and credentials:** add any keys the project needs through the repository's or harness's secret store.
  They never go in the repository, and setting them is always a manual owner step.
  If this project syncs from a private `_src_path`, add `UPSTREAM_SRC_READ_TOKEN` (a token with read access to that source) so `review-gate-check.yml`'s SDLC-hold check can clone it; leave it unset for a public source, where the check clones without it as before.
- [ ] **Revoke the bootstrap token** once the script has run.

## Harness follow-ups

- [ ] Add the repository to the coordinator's configured repository list.
- [ ] Paste the text between the markers in `docs/agents/coordinator-core-snippet.md` into the harness's project-level instructions, after the owner's scope section and an empty `## Coordinator notes` zone, then start the coordinator session; it loads `.forge/coordinator-core.md` itself and runs its own self-check. Re-paste whenever the snippet changes (`python3 scripts/check_coordinator_core.py drift <file holding the live instructions>` reports drift).
- [ ] Install the harness's GitHub App (or equivalent) on this repository only, so agent sessions can push branches and open PRs.
- [ ] Stand up the Main Health thread (`.agents/skills/watch-main-ci/SKILL.md`): it schedules the post-merge review pass, the queue sweep and, once the project writes it, the local full-suite check.
- [ ] Map the capability tiers to models in `.forge/model-tiers.md` if the defaults do not suit the harness, recording the change in `docs/forge-overrides.md`.

## Then: stage 0

- [ ] Ask the agents to run stage 0 (`.forge/feature-pipeline.md`): the grilling interview that seeds `docs/principles.md`, settles the real tools behind the guard stubs (lint, dead code, size caps, dependency pins, dependency audit), sets the coverage floor from a measured baseline, and the setup, test and lint commands, and offers the `impeccable` setup if the project has a user interface.
  `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` already pins its base image to a digest; when stage 0 replaces a placeholder image, keep it pinned to a digest too (`.forge/code-shape-rules.md`, "Pinned dependencies").
